# What `docker build` never sends from this directory — the build context of
# the app, migrator and ops images (Dockerfile) and of db-writer's
# (workers/db-writer/Dockerfile.writer).
#
# The Dockerfile's builder stage runs `COPY . .`, so without this file
# everything here is in that stage, and `next build` reads .env and
# .env.production from it, which Next's standalone output then copies into the
# runner image that ships. This is the machine that deploys, so it is also where
# the deploy's rendered env files, the vault password and any vault somebody
# decrypted sit. The image needs none of them: its settings arrive as the
# container's environment at run time. scripts/check_image_contents.sh in the
# template repository plants each of these and fails if any reaches an image.
#
# Nothing the build needs is here: the Dockerfile copies package.json,
# package-lock.json, tsconfig.json, drizzle.config.ts, lib/, scripts/ and
# workers/db-writer/, and `next build` reads app/, components/, content/,
# lib/, public/, types/ and the config files at the root.

# Secrets. Every env file at any depth — the operator's own (.env,
# .env.local, .env.production), the ones a deploy renders (.env-production,
# .env-app and the rest), and .env.example, which nothing in a build reads.
**/.env*
**/.vault-pass
**/*.pem
**/*.key
# The Ansible tree holds the vault, encrypted or not, and the vault password's
# usual home. No image uses any of it.
ansible/

# Dependencies. Each image installs its own with a frozen `npm ci`; the host's
# would land on top of that install and the image would run whatever this
# machine happened to have.
**/node_modules

# Local build output. The builder stage runs `next build` itself, and a stale
# .next or incremental-build record from here would only confuse it.
.next/
out/
build/
dist/
cli/dist/
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Test, coverage and Python artefacts.
coverage/
.nyc_output/
test-results/
playwright-report/
blob-report/
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache
**/.venv

# Everything else that is only ever local: history, image exports a deploy
# saved, Caddy's access log bind-mounted out of the production stack, and
# package-manager debug logs.
.git/
**/*.tar.gz
logs/
**/*.log
